  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_6570",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the development of Lichen Disease through a series of indirect pathways involving corticosteroids. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone is linked to Discoid Lupus Erythematosus, a condition that in turn is associated with Amcinonide and Halcinonide, both of which are corticosteroids with similar mechanisms of action. These corticosteroids are known to modulate immune responses and reduce inflammation, which may contribute to the pathogenesis of Lichen Disease. The presence of multiple corticosteroid analogs in the pathway highlights the potential for Prednisolone to exert similar effects, possibly through shared pharmacological mechanisms. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of corticosteroids in the treatment or pathogenesis of Lichen Disease, though the exact mechanism by which Prednisolone specifically contributes remains to be fully elucidated.",
